8. PAUSE, RESUME, CLOSE, AND SESSION MANAGEMENT

The assistant must have clearly distinguishable pause and close operations.

Pause

When the user pauses:

- Stop microphone recording.
- Stop sending new audio.
- Stop AI response playback.
- Cancel or suspend active work safely.
- Preserve conversation history.
- Update UI status to Paused.
- Do not unexpectedly restart microphone recording.

Define whether the WebSocket session remains connected or is suspended based on API capabilities and resource considerations.

Resume

When the user resumes:

- Restore the required session state.
- Reconnect if the session has expired.
- Preserve previous conversation context.
- Start listening only after the user explicitly resumes or starts a new request.

Close

When the user closes the assistant:

- Stop recording.
- Stop playback.
- Cancel active coroutines.
- Cancel pending response jobs.
- Close or release the session according to the session policy.
- Release audio resources.
- Update the state to Closed.
- Keep conversation history according to the configured session-retention policy.

Closing the assistant UI must not accidentally leave the microphone active.

Define the difference between hiding the assistant interface and terminating the conversation session.

Provide predictable behavior.

