9. ANDROID APPLICATION LIFECYCLE MANAGEMENT

Handle lifecycle transitions carefully.

The application must never continue playing voice responses unexpectedly when it is minimized or no longer visible.

When application enters background

When the application goes to background:

- Stop microphone recording.
- Stop outgoing audio streaming.
- Stop AI audio playback immediately.
- Cancel or suspend active audio operations safely.
- Update assistant state.
- Prevent audio from unexpectedly playing.
- Preserve conversation context.
- Avoid leaking microphone resources.
- Avoid leaving a WebSocket session in an inconsistent state.

When application returns to foreground

- Restore the assistant interface if it was open.
- Restore the previous conversation history.
- Check whether the session is still valid.
- Reconnect only when appropriate.
- Display the correct connection status.
- Do not automatically start recording unless explicitly allowed by the user and permission/session state.

Lifecycle architecture

Use appropriate lifecycle-aware components.

Do not tie the entire conversation session to an individual screen's lifecycle.

Use a shared application-scoped session manager where appropriate, while ensuring that the microphone and playback are controlled according to the foreground lifecycle.

Do not use a foreground service just to keep the assistant speaking in the background.

Do not introduce background audio behavior that the user has not explicitly requested.

