13. THREADING, PERFORMANCE, ANR, AND MEMORY MANAGEMENT

Performance and stability are critical.

The implementation must not cause ANRs, memory leaks, excessive battery usage, or memory exhaustion.

Main thread

Never perform these operations on the main thread:

- Audio recording.
- Audio encoding/decoding.
- WebSocket message processing.
- Large JSON parsing.
- Audio buffering.
- AI response processing.
- Blocking network operations.
- Heavy conversation processing.

Use appropriate dispatchers and structured concurrency.

Memory management

Handle:

- Bounded audio input buffers.
- Bounded audio output buffers.
- Bounded conversation history.
- Proper cancellation.
- No unbounded channels.
- No unlimited message queues.
- No unnecessary byte-array copying.
- No retained Activity references.
- No duplicated audio streams.
- No leaked WebSocket listeners.
- No stale ViewModel jobs.
- No orphaned audio resources.

Avoid retaining large audio data after playback.

Release resources when the session is closed.

Use backpressure instead of allowing incoming data to grow indefinitely.

Battery and resource usage

- Avoid unnecessary reconnect loops.
- Avoid unnecessary audio processing.
- Avoid recording while paused or closed.
- Avoid unnecessary background operations.
- Avoid keeping resources active when the assistant is not in use.

